an player may trade it too easily or something maybe (i am not sure about this change change but maybe it will work out well in overall diplomacy and allow for more startegy rather than easy trade abuse/exploit anyways etc)). Note: coastal bonuses have a more moderate version of this as we assume many cities are not coastal so they would not gain the building related bonus's extra effect quite often. We count it as such even in water heavy maps (treated the same to simplify anyways etc), so fish would be worth more than pig (with as of now harbor but anyways etc) but less than maize or wheat for example anyways etc. See [66 - (Fixed and greatly enhanced) AI overvaluing bonuses that give minor effects such as pig or cattle/cow (+1 health only), etc, that AI would value the same as maize or wheat (+2 health effectively since almost all cities have a granary and very early anyways etc) or grapes (from grocer) or molluscs (from harbor) for example, by adding a pre-check in CvPlayerAI::AI_bonusTradeVal to value relatively more bonuses the more effects they provide from buildings if we have their required tech of these buildings, so that humans can't abuse/exploit it with aggressive trading to become super rich xd if i may say but anyways etc, and also in AI vs AI trading each AI gets best or more value out of the effective value of their bonuses at least more so now if i may say but anyways etc](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs_And_Appendixes/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#66---fixed-and-greatly-enhanced-ai-overvaluing-bonuses-that-give-minor-effects-such-as-pig-or-cattlecow-1-health-only-etc-that-ai-would-value-the-same-as-maize-or-wheat-2-health-effectively-since-almost-all-cities-have-a-granary-and-very-early-anyways-etc-or-grapes-from-grocer-or-molluscs-from-harbor-for-example-by-adding-a-pre-check-in-cvplayeraiai_bonustradeval-to-value-relatively-more-bonuses-the-more-effects-they-provide-from-buildings-if-we-have-their-required-tech-of-these-buildings-so-that-humans